You are an advanced AI coding assistant.

## Project

This is a personal website (coderonfire.com) built with **Eleventy (11ty) v3**, a static site generator.
The package manager is **pnpm**. Strict TypeScript is used.

## Folder Structure

```
pages/               → Eleventy input directory (`.md` files → HTML output)
  _includes/         → Nunjucks (.njk) and Liquid (.liquid) layout templates
    base.njk         → Main page layout
    video.liquid     → Video embed partial
  work/              → Work/project pages, tagged "Work", sorted by `weight` front matter
  pages.json         → Global front-matter defaults (layout: base.njk)
static/              → Passthrough-copied to site root (fonts, images, video, PDFs, etc.)
  css/main.css       → CSS entry point, bundled by esbuild into _site/css/bundle.css
  ts/                → TypeScript entry point, bundled by esbuild into _site/bundle.js
    main.ts          → App entry, imports all modules
    boxes.ts         → WebGL 3D box animation (ogl library, GLSL shaders)
    boxes-debug.ts   → Debug GUI (lil-gui), dynamically imported only in dev
    slide-images.ts  → IntersectionObserver-based scroll animations
    video-controls.ts→ Custom video player controls
```

## Build Pipeline

- **Templates**: Nunjucks (`.njk`) and Liquid (`.liquid`) in `pages/_includes/`
- **TypeScript**: Entry `static/ts/main.ts` → esbuild bundles to `_site/bundle.js`
  - Format: IIFE, target: ES2020, minified, sourcemaps enabled
- **CSS**: Entry `static/css/main.css` → esbuild bundles to `_site/css/bundle.css`
  - Font/image/icon URLs are external (not inlined)
- **Images**: `@11ty/eleventy-img` plugin auto-optimizes `<img>` tags (AVIF/JPEG, responsive widths)
- **Global define**: `__DEV__` is `true` in dev/watch mode, `false` in production builds
- **Static assets**: Everything in `static/` is copied to site root via `addPassthroughCopy`

## Tools

| Command         | Purpose                          |
|-----------------|----------------------------------|
| `pnpm dev`      | Start dev server with hot reload |
| `pnpm build`    | Production build                 |
| `pnpm lint`     | Lint with oxlint                 |
| `pnpm format`   | Format with oxfmt                |

## Key Patterns

### WebGL / Shaders
- Uses the `ogl` library for WebGL rendering
- GLSL shader code is inline in template literals within `boxes.ts`
- Debug UI (`lil-gui`) is **dynamically imported** only when `__DEV__ && ?dev` URL param is present
- Never ship debug code to production bundles

### Front Matter & Collections
- Page metadata (title, description, image, weight, tags) lives in YAML front matter
- `pages.json` sets global defaults (e.g., `layout: base.njk`)
- Work pages are tagged `"Work"` and sorted by a numeric `weight` field
- Social/OG images use a custom `socialImage` async filter for processing

### CSS
- Use `eleventyConfig.addBundle("css")` for page-specific CSS in templates
- Global styles go in `static/css/main.css`

### DOM / Browser APIs
- Use `AbortController` with `signal` option for clean event listener cleanup
- Use `IntersectionObserver` for scroll-triggered animations
- Use `AbortController` to tear down WebGL canvases and debug GUIs

## Code Style

- Comments go on their own line (not inline after code)
- Prefer multi-line arrow functions with brackets `() => { ... }` over single-expression form
- Prefer modern JavaScript and Browser DOM APIs (`AbortController`, `IntersectionObserver`, etc.)
- Follow industry best practices and clean code principles but do not over-engineer
- TypeScript: avoid `any`, use strict types, avoid `as` casts when possible
- Linting rules are defined in `.oxlintrc.json` — follow them
